# Every fusion of one part that eliminates nothing, beside the part it carries. One row per such
# fusion per quantity, `violates` where the composed figure is not the part's.
#
# One part, nothing eliminated, carried unchanged
#   The rule: a fusion of one part with nothing eliminated carries that part unchanged. There is
#   nothing to add, nothing to subtract and no judgement to make, so a difference here has no
#   defence. `every-local-part` states the case it tests: a one-part fusion says this reviewer
#   read that layer and carried it. Carrying is an assertion, and so something that can be got
#   wrong.
#
# The only rule on a composed slack
#   `fusion_sum_disagrees` reads `composition/fused.sqlc`, which covers the demand, the nameplate
#   and the draw, and `window_lost_or_summed` covers the calendar. The three slacks are compared
#   here and nowhere else, so without this rule a one-part fusion's composed slack could move and
#   no composition rule would notice.
#
# What it does not cover
#   It covers only the case where the arithmetic is trivial. A multi-part fusion's slacks are
#   compared by no rule.
#
# Figures, not units
#   A single part may be converted into the composed layer's unit, and a unit that differs is what
#   `asrt:factor` is for. The figure is compared after conversion; `quantum_unit_mismatch` and
#   `slack_unit_mismatch` own the units.
#
# Suspension is inherited, not restated
#   composition/carried.sqlc excludes anything suspended and anything with an elimination filed,
#   so this rule never has to decide what is owed: it examines only the fusions where the answer
#   is forced.
#
# Probe
#   Move the composed nameplate of `merge-group-composition/compute-us` to five times the one part
#   it is composed from; this rule must fire.
-- composition/carried.sqlc: the part's figure against the composed layer's, per quantity.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT c.filing, c.layer,
           abs(c.part_low  - c.filed_low)  > 1e-9
        OR abs(c.part_mode - c.filed_mode) > 1e-9
        OR abs(c.part_high - c.filed_high) > 1e-9                    AS violates,
           format('%s carried as [%s, %s, %s] against a part of [%s, %s, %s]',
                  c.quantity, c.filed_low, c.filed_mode, c.filed_high,
                  c.part_low, c.part_mode, c.part_high)              AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(composition/carried.sqlc)
    ) c
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'one_part_fusion_alters_its_part'
